1
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,940
[The Lament of Autumn]

2
00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:41,759
[Episode 9]

3
00:01:41,979 --> 00:01:49,250
[Security Office] [Quartermaster's Office]

4
00:01:49,310 --> 00:01:49,630
[Secretariat] [Inspector General's Office]

5
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:52,289
[Dispatch Room]
[Inspector General's Office]

6
00:01:55,090 --> 00:01:56,000
[Quartermaster's Office]

7
00:01:57,420 --> 00:01:58,590
[Secretariat]

8
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:02,220
[Reception Office]

9
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:03,010
[Reference Room]

10
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:12,270
[Archives]

11
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:24,410
Secretary Jiang.

12
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:26,400
You should put

13
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:27,960
your documents in the Reference Room.

14
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:29,160
This is the Archives.

15
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:33,079
I'm new here, so I'm still
finding my way around.

16
00:02:33,079 --> 00:02:33,900
I need to access some files,

17
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:34,460
though.

18
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:36,410
How do I apply for that?

19
00:02:43,150 --> 00:02:43,710
Good.

20
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:45,680
Here.

21
00:02:47,579 --> 00:02:48,579
Staff Officer Li.

22
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:50,880
I need to access

23
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,300
some reference materials.

24
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:54,790
Team Leader Bao said
I had to get your signature.

25
00:02:54,790 --> 00:02:55,410
You could've just left these

26
00:02:55,410 --> 00:02:56,500
in my office.

27
00:02:56,690 --> 00:02:59,020
Why come all the way
to the shooting range?

28
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:01,590
I went to your office,

29
00:03:01,870 --> 00:03:02,770
but you weren't there.

30
00:03:02,770 --> 00:03:06,220
[Ever Loyal and Unwavering in Courage]

31
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,150
The previous paperwork

32
00:03:04,150 --> 00:03:05,500
still hasn't been signed, either,

33
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:07,560
so I had no choice but to come find you.

34
00:03:08,130 --> 00:03:08,730
That's it.

35
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:09,660
Keep it up,

36
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:10,560
guys.

37
00:03:11,530 --> 00:03:12,530
Steady, alright?

38
00:03:14,690 --> 00:03:15,690
Staff Officer Li.

39
00:03:18,070 --> 00:03:18,670
Let me see.

40
00:03:22,150 --> 00:03:23,900
[Reason: Request for
Specific Translation Reference Materials]

41
00:03:25,370 --> 00:03:26,070
No rush.

42
00:03:26,970 --> 00:03:27,310
Right.

43
00:03:27,310 --> 00:03:28,360
Hold on a little longer.

44
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:29,690
Sweat more in training,

45
00:03:29,930 --> 00:03:31,570
bleed less in battle!

46
00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:47,230
Secretary Jiang.

47
00:03:48,180 --> 00:03:48,530
Since you rarely

48
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:49,910
come to the shooting range,

49
00:03:49,910 --> 00:03:50,630
why don't we

50
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:52,600
have a little contest?

51
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:54,620
Staff Officer Li.

52
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:56,130
I'm not very good at this.

53
00:03:56,130 --> 00:03:57,260
I'm no match for you.

54
00:03:57,780 --> 00:03:58,890
Secretary Jiang.

55
00:03:59,130 --> 00:04:00,500
I've already seen

56
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,130
how talented you are with words.

57
00:04:02,130 --> 00:04:03,130
I'm sure shooting

58
00:04:03,530 --> 00:04:05,590
is a piece of cake for you, too, right?

59
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:06,720
How about this?

60
00:04:07,530 --> 00:04:08,590
Let's have a match.

61
00:04:08,630 --> 00:04:09,740
If you win,

62
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:11,360
I'll sign it right away.

63
00:04:11,630 --> 00:04:12,760
How does that sound?

64
00:04:22,390 --> 00:04:23,520
Alright. Let's do it

65
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:25,720
your way then, Staff Officer Li.

66
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:45,740
Staff Officer Li,

67
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:47,130
25 points in total!

68
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:49,360
Impressive!

69
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:50,820
Just what I'd expect from
Staff Officer Li.

70
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:51,590
Indeed.

71
00:04:51,590 --> 00:04:52,800
Nice shot.

72
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:54,270
Secretary Jiang.

73
00:04:54,270 --> 00:04:55,180
I haven't practiced in so long,

74
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:56,440
so my aim's a bit rusty.

75
00:04:57,620 --> 00:04:58,620
Secretary Jiang.

76
00:04:59,070 --> 00:04:59,670
Your turn.

77
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:08,480
Seven points!

78
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:11,310
Staff Officer Li,

79
00:05:11,310 --> 00:05:12,970
sorry to make a fool of myself.

80
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:13,900
It's okay.

81
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:15,760
Don't be nervous.

82
00:05:15,890 --> 00:05:16,680
Just relax.

83
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:18,860
Besides, I don't think

84
00:05:18,930 --> 00:05:19,330
7 points

85
00:05:19,330 --> 00:05:20,730
is all you're capable of.

86
00:05:20,810 --> 00:05:22,070
Show us what you've got

87
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,570
and let everyone see what you can do.

88
00:05:23,570 --> 00:05:24,030
Come on.

89
00:05:38,180 --> 00:05:39,310
Nine points?

90
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:41,630
For real?

91
00:05:42,130 --> 00:05:43,550
How's he that good?

92
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:46,050
Not bad.

93
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:47,870
See? I-I told you good luck

94
00:05:47,870 --> 00:05:49,500
would eventually come your way,

95
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:49,900
right?

96
00:05:49,909 --> 00:05:52,640
I owe it to your encouragement,
Staff Officer Li.

97
00:05:52,890 --> 00:05:54,420
I've got one last shot left.

98
00:06:08,890 --> 00:06:09,550
Ten points!

99
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:11,330
Ten points?

100
00:06:11,420 --> 00:06:12,220
Ten points?

101
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:14,370
No way.

102
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:15,990
Secretary Jiang is clearly an expert.

103
00:06:15,990 --> 00:06:19,120
Otherwise, there's no way
he could've hit the bullseye.

104
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:22,330
You were messing with me just now,
weren't you?

105
00:06:22,330 --> 00:06:23,330
It was just a game.

106
00:06:23,430 --> 00:06:24,660
A bit of fun, that's all.

107
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:25,540
A bit of fun?

108
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,290
You brat.

109
00:06:28,450 --> 00:06:29,790
You were acting like
a frightened rabbit just now,

110
00:06:29,790 --> 00:06:31,080
and now you're making fun of me?

111
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:31,740
You...

112
00:06:32,390 --> 00:06:34,370
You're making a mockery of your superior!

113
00:06:34,370 --> 00:06:34,890
You...

114
00:06:37,010 --> 00:06:40,650
[Ever Loyal and Unwavering in Courage]

115
00:06:38,070 --> 00:06:38,750
Nice shot.

116
00:06:38,770 --> 00:06:41,030
-Hello, Commander.
-Hello, Commander.

117
00:06:41,930 --> 00:06:42,590
Commander.

118
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:43,860
Secretary Jiang,

119
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:45,860
I see you're a warrior-scholar.

120
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:47,520
I remember your resume stated

121
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,240
that you once studied combat

122
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,750
at a school in Japan, right?

123
00:06:49,750 --> 00:06:51,110
How about a little

124
00:06:51,890 --> 00:06:52,820
sparring match?

125
00:06:55,430 --> 00:06:56,960
You flatter me, Commander.

126
00:06:57,659 --> 00:06:58,659
It's just a hobby.

127
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:00,360
Secretary Jiang,

128
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:02,750
you're so modest.

129
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:06,730
Or do you think I'm no match for you?

130
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:20,680
Secretary Jiang.

131
00:07:21,410 --> 00:07:22,940
Don't you dare go easy on me.

132
00:07:23,190 --> 00:07:24,590
Against you, Commander,

133
00:07:24,830 --> 00:07:26,290
I'll have to give it my all.

134
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:28,620
Otherwise, I might not make it out alive.

135
00:07:28,940 --> 00:07:29,330
Good.

136
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:31,600
That's the fighting spirit

137
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:32,920
I want in my men.

138
00:07:34,020 --> 00:07:35,610
But today, we're not
fighting to the death—

139
00:07:35,610 --> 00:07:36,540
just wrestling.

140
00:07:37,010 --> 00:07:37,800
Whoever gets thrown out of the ring

141
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:38,680
or is taken down

142
00:07:38,810 --> 00:07:39,360
loses.

143
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:09,560
Bravo!

144
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:10,450
Nice!

145
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:11,840
Wonderful!

146
00:08:20,330 --> 00:08:22,300
-Nice!
-Wonderful!

147
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:28,660
Well done, Commander! Impressive!

148
00:08:34,210 --> 00:08:35,409
Still not convinced?

149
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:36,669
Just admit defeat if you can't win.

150
00:08:36,669 --> 00:08:38,799
You were already thrown to the ground.

151
00:09:46,060 --> 00:09:47,270
Secretary Jiang.

152
00:09:47,570 --> 00:09:49,100
You're truly a rare talent,

153
00:09:49,890 --> 00:09:51,750
skilled in both brains and brawn.

154
00:09:53,130 --> 00:09:54,730
You're too kind, Commander.

155
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:56,900
I've been thrown down several times,

156
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:58,680
and my foot crossed the line.

157
00:09:58,740 --> 00:09:59,200
By the rules

158
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,320
I learned in Japan,

159
00:10:00,890 --> 00:10:01,980
I've already lost.

160
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:04,250
We're in a Chinese military camp.

161
00:10:04,250 --> 00:10:06,050
We don't follow Japanese rules.

162
00:10:06,830 --> 00:10:08,270
Let's call it a draw.

163
00:10:09,530 --> 00:10:10,160
Boren.

164
00:10:11,650 --> 00:10:12,850
Put in a merit for him.

165
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:16,380
That counts as a merit?

166
00:10:18,310 --> 00:10:20,110
Fine, I'll practice later, too.

167
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:32,130
Auntie.

168
00:10:32,870 --> 00:10:34,100
I specially brought

169
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:35,200
this Master Cai all the way here

170
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,080
from Suzhou.

171
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:37,650
His family has made embroidered garments

172
00:10:37,650 --> 00:10:39,340
for the imperial court for 3 generations.

173
00:10:39,340 --> 00:10:41,030
His craftsmanship is second to none.

174
00:10:41,030 --> 00:10:43,620
You really know
how to take care of things.

175
00:10:45,130 --> 00:10:45,870
Third Madam,

176
00:10:45,910 --> 00:10:47,080
you really look good

177
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:48,280
in anything you wear.

178
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:49,250
Really?

179
00:10:49,630 --> 00:10:50,130
I was just feeling guilty

180
00:10:50,130 --> 00:10:51,590
about gaining some weight

181
00:10:52,030 --> 00:10:53,120
since autumn started.

182
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,820
If you call that gaining weight,

183
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:56,050
then I'm a whole granary

184
00:10:56,050 --> 00:10:57,870
storing up food for winter.

185
00:10:59,530 --> 00:11:01,000
You're just blessed with a generous heart

186
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,530
and a well-rounded figure.

187
00:11:02,820 --> 00:11:04,480
You really know how to flatter people

188
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:06,610
with that sweet little mouth of yours.

189
00:11:07,340 --> 00:11:07,980
Ziyi.

190
00:11:08,220 --> 00:11:09,530
You must've heard

191
00:11:09,630 --> 00:11:10,820
that Nanhuai has recently taken in

192
00:11:10,820 --> 00:11:11,860
a group of refugees.

193
00:11:11,860 --> 00:11:13,510
The Charity Union is planning to establish

194
00:11:13,510 --> 00:11:14,640
a new orphanage.

195
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:15,790
Mom has been busy lately

196
00:11:15,790 --> 00:11:17,390
finding a suitable site for the orphanage

197
00:11:17,390 --> 00:11:19,650
and coordinating with various parties.

198
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:24,860
Auntie, you're so kind and charitable.

199
00:11:24,860 --> 00:11:25,840
There's still so much

200
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,320
I can learn from you.

201
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:29,550
Mom.

202
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:32,820
The one who petitioned for the refugees,

203
00:11:32,820 --> 00:11:33,480
Ye Pingjun,

204
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:35,070
do you still remember her?

205
00:11:35,220 --> 00:11:36,320
She and Ziyi

206
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,620
were actually classmates

207
00:11:37,620 --> 00:11:39,150
at Mingde School, you know.

208
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:41,340
Is that so?

209
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:43,820
But

210
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:46,400
you two have such different hobbies.

211
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:48,630
What a contrast.

212
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:54,750
Auntie.

213
00:11:55,130 --> 00:11:56,460
Qixuan is right.

214
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:58,470
We each have our own strengths

215
00:11:58,500 --> 00:11:59,500
and do what we can.

216
00:12:00,150 --> 00:12:00,860
I'll ask my father

217
00:12:00,860 --> 00:12:02,120
to order a batch of supplies

218
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:03,980
to distribute to the refugees, too.

219
00:12:03,980 --> 00:12:05,320
That would be great.

220
00:12:05,370 --> 00:12:06,870
How thoughtful of you, Ziyi.

221
00:12:06,870 --> 00:12:08,130
It's the least I can do.

222
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:09,960
Auntie.

223
00:12:10,250 --> 00:12:12,310
Check out this fabric. Do you like it?

224
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:13,650
It's pretty.

225
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:14,390
What is it?

226
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:16,080
Watch what you say.

227
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:18,880
One day,

228
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:21,280
she might be your fifth sister-in-law.

229
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,260
Let me tell you, Minru,

230
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:25,480
this Tao Ziyi is such a phony.

231
00:12:25,740 --> 00:12:27,080
She spends all day at school

232
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,860
throwing her weight around
with a bunch of so-called rich girls,

233
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:30,170
bullying others.

234
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:32,240
She thinks no one knows,

235
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:34,360
but I can't stand that kind of behavior.

236
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:36,120
I don't want her to be
my fifth sister-in-law.

237
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:39,180
That still doesn't give you the right
to talk like that.

238
00:12:40,030 --> 00:12:41,090
Alright, alright.

239
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:41,840
I'll stop.

240
00:12:52,030 --> 00:12:52,700
Xueting.

241
00:12:55,050 --> 00:12:55,720
Xueting?

242
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:57,060
Coming.

243
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:03,630
Here.

244
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:06,420
What delicious food did Auntie make again?

245
00:13:06,510 --> 00:13:08,740
Mom made pan-fried tofu today,

246
00:13:09,220 --> 00:13:10,510
and Mrs. Zhao made some buns.

247
00:13:10,510 --> 00:13:12,170
These are all your favorites.

248
00:13:14,030 --> 00:13:15,690
I'll pour you a glass of water.

249
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:40,080
Xueting.

250
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:43,810
Are you injured?

251
00:13:49,890 --> 00:13:51,090
Just a minor scratch.

252
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:53,100
Let me see.

253
00:13:56,740 --> 00:13:58,390
How did you get hurt like this?

254
00:13:58,390 --> 00:13:59,260
What happened?

255
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:02,340
Just a regular sparring match
at the military camp.

256
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:03,530
But you're a civilian employee.

257
00:14:03,530 --> 00:14:05,530
Why would they want to spar with you?

258
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:12,160
Don't worry about it.

259
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:13,340
I agreed to it

260
00:14:13,820 --> 00:14:14,700
myself.

261
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:17,460
Come here.

262
00:14:17,790 --> 00:14:19,850
I'll help you put some ointment on it.

263
00:14:23,590 --> 00:14:25,090
Here, put your hand here.

264
00:14:29,820 --> 00:14:31,120
Tell me if it hurts.

265
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:48,980
Does it still hurt?

266
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:51,190
Not anymore.

267
00:14:51,870 --> 00:14:53,500
With you tending to my wounds,

268
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:54,750
they'll all heal.

269
00:15:03,740 --> 00:15:05,400
Your shoulder's injured too.

270
00:15:06,370 --> 00:15:07,370
Let me take a look.

271
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:11,150
Careful.

272
00:15:15,010 --> 00:15:16,070
Tell me if it hurts.

273
00:15:36,510 --> 00:15:37,170
Mr. Yu.

274
00:15:37,990 --> 00:15:39,140
Please wait.

275
00:15:46,650 --> 00:15:47,910
Can we talk in private?

276
00:15:52,390 --> 00:15:54,200
Miss Ye, you came specifically to see me.

277
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,730
Is there something urgent?

278
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:56,670
Did you guys

279
00:15:56,670 --> 00:15:58,800
intentionally injure Jiang Xueting?

280
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:00,710
You mean Secretary Jiang?

281
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:02,030
You two know each other?

282
00:16:02,030 --> 00:16:03,210
Stop pretending.

283
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:04,720
You already know

284
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,720
about our relationship, don't you?

285
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:09,090
What relationship?

286
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:11,300
Why don't you tell me?

287
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,460
Could it be

288
00:16:17,150 --> 00:16:18,350
that he's your lover?

289
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:23,130
It's none of your business.

290
00:16:24,130 --> 00:16:25,270
I just want to know

291
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:26,930
why a civilian secretary

292
00:16:26,930 --> 00:16:29,530
would have to participate in
a sparring match.

293
00:16:29,890 --> 00:16:31,670
Whether civilian or military,

294
00:16:32,290 --> 00:16:33,990
all soldiers in my Ninth Army

295
00:16:34,330 --> 00:16:36,060
take part in regular training.

296
00:16:36,180 --> 00:16:38,040
It's perfectly normal to get hurt

297
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,860
during hand-to-hand combat.

298
00:16:40,320 --> 00:16:41,510
If you're holding a grudge against me

299
00:16:41,510 --> 00:16:42,360
because I slapped you

300
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:43,490
at the refugee camp,

301
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,060
I've already apologized.

302
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:47,350
If you still can't let it go,

303
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,440
then go ahead and hit me back.

304
00:16:56,340 --> 00:16:57,030
Seriously?

305
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:04,210
You won't regret it?

306
00:17:07,089 --> 00:17:07,680
I won't.

307
00:17:11,660 --> 00:17:12,460
Alright then.

308
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:15,920
I hit pretty hard,

309
00:17:21,319 --> 00:17:22,380
so brace yourself.

310
00:17:30,350 --> 00:17:30,990
Go ahead.

311
00:18:47,650 --> 00:18:48,710
What are you doing?

312
00:18:50,510 --> 00:18:52,710
Well, I'm still a gentleman, after all.

313
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:55,220
How could I bear

314
00:18:56,150 --> 00:18:57,610
to hurt such a pretty face?

315
00:19:02,070 --> 00:19:03,070
Secretary Jiang.

316
00:19:04,770 --> 00:19:05,770
Secretary Jiang.

317
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,060
Xueting.

318
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:12,930
Pingjun?

319
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:15,560
Commander.

320
00:19:18,650 --> 00:19:19,980
What are you doing here?

321
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:23,960
Secretary Jiang.

322
00:19:24,890 --> 00:19:26,090
I only found out today

323
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:28,260
that Miss Ye is your girlfriend.

324
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:33,070
She never told you

325
00:19:33,070 --> 00:19:34,070
that she knows me?

326
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:39,850
Pingjun did.

327
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:41,390
She said you two

328
00:19:41,420 --> 00:19:42,930
once had a misunderstanding
at Xiangxi Hotel,

329
00:19:42,930 --> 00:19:44,240
but you'd cleared things up

330
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:46,060
and had nothing more to do
with each other.

331
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:47,460
That's what she told you?

332
00:19:53,330 --> 00:19:54,240
But misunderstandings

333
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:56,300
don't seem to be that easy to clear up.

334
00:19:56,390 --> 00:19:57,510
She saw you injured

335
00:19:57,530 --> 00:19:59,660
and immediately assumed I'd bullied you.

336
00:19:59,660 --> 00:20:01,430
She even came all the way here

337
00:20:02,370 --> 00:20:04,700
to accuse me of throwing my weight around.

338
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:08,140
It's my fault

339
00:20:08,330 --> 00:20:10,660
for not explaining it clearly to Pingjun.

340
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:12,140
I'm partly to blame, too.

341
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:14,210
I did get a little carried away.

342
00:20:14,460 --> 00:20:15,320
How about this?

343
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:17,000
Since we're off work anyway,

344
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,060
to make it up to you,

345
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:20,220
I'll drive you both home myself.

346
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:20,950
No need.

347
00:20:26,720 --> 00:20:27,440
We wouldn't want to

348
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:28,720
trouble you, Mr. Yu.

349
00:20:28,850 --> 00:20:29,380
Exactly.

350
00:20:29,860 --> 00:20:31,390
We'll make our own way home.

351
00:20:31,530 --> 00:20:32,130
What,

352
00:20:33,530 --> 00:20:34,530
you won't even give me a chance

353
00:20:34,530 --> 00:20:35,400
to apologize?

354
00:21:01,740 --> 00:21:03,180
Secretary Jiang, Miss Ye.

355
00:21:03,180 --> 00:21:04,840
You two make a perfect couple.

356
00:21:04,970 --> 00:21:06,960
Have you been neighbors since childhood?

357
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:08,720
Our mothers were the closest of friends

358
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:09,780
and sworn sisters,

359
00:21:10,270 --> 00:21:10,900
so Pingjun and I

360
00:21:10,900 --> 00:21:11,930
grew up together.

361
00:21:13,660 --> 00:21:15,590
So you were betrothed as children?

362
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:17,200
That's right.

363
00:21:18,220 --> 00:21:20,420
Miss Ye is both beautiful and talented.

364
00:21:20,530 --> 00:21:21,660
How could you bear to

365
00:21:22,090 --> 00:21:24,570
leave such a wonderful girlfriend alone
for 4 years?

366
00:21:24,570 --> 00:21:26,020
Weren't you worried

367
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:28,130
someone else might steal her away?

368
00:21:29,570 --> 00:21:31,310
My mother taught me from a young age

369
00:21:31,310 --> 00:21:33,250
that once you've made up your mind
about someone or something,

370
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:35,070
you shouldn't divide your attention

371
00:21:35,070 --> 00:21:36,600
or keep changing your mind.

372
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:38,960
Such unwavering devotion

373
00:21:39,120 --> 00:21:40,250
is truly admirable.

374
00:21:46,110 --> 00:21:46,770
Commander,

375
00:21:46,830 --> 00:21:47,850
turn right at the intersection ahead.

376
00:21:47,850 --> 00:21:48,430
I know.

377
00:21:58,770 --> 00:22:00,260
When Miss Ye was ill,

378
00:22:00,280 --> 00:22:03,110
I once delivered medicine to her
on Lan Qing's behalf.

379
00:22:03,110 --> 00:22:03,720
Xueting,

380
00:22:04,110 --> 00:22:05,290
you didn't know this,

381
00:22:05,290 --> 00:22:07,020
but Mr. Yu is an expert on opera,

382
00:22:07,070 --> 00:22:08,960
and he's a longtime fan of Miss Lan Qing.

383
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:09,820
You flatter me.

384
00:22:10,590 --> 00:22:12,720
Miss Ye was also
quite the celebrated talent

385
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:14,270
at Yuchun Theater.

386
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:16,010
When she resigned,

387
00:22:16,070 --> 00:22:18,130
everyone was reluctant to see her go.

388
00:22:20,270 --> 00:22:21,470
I'm ashamed to say it,

389
00:22:22,140 --> 00:22:24,470
but if I'd returned from overseas sooner,

390
00:22:25,530 --> 00:22:28,590
Pingjun wouldn't have had to

391
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:31,080
juggle school and work at the same time.

392
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:39,060
You two are such a devoted couple.

393
00:22:39,070 --> 00:22:40,270
It's truly enviable.

394
00:22:50,110 --> 00:22:50,770
Commander.

395
00:22:51,530 --> 00:22:52,530
It's still early.

396
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:54,330
If you don't mind,

397
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:56,610
why don't we have a cup of tea together?

398
00:22:57,740 --> 00:22:58,670
Maybe next time.

399
00:22:59,090 --> 00:23:01,160
I still have to go home to feed my birds.

400
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:02,140
Those canaries

401
00:23:02,900 --> 00:23:04,040
are quite a handful.

402
00:23:05,030 --> 00:23:05,560
Alright.

403
00:23:06,920 --> 00:23:07,450
Pingjun.

404
00:23:09,090 --> 00:23:09,620
Let's go.

405
00:23:10,570 --> 00:23:11,040
Okay.

406
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:48,110
You're just impossible to please.

407
00:23:48,710 --> 00:23:50,440
I've really spoiled you rotten

408
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:57,930
and let you get away
with this terrible attitude.

409
00:24:07,420 --> 00:24:09,550
You don't like the birdcage I gave you,

410
00:24:14,750 --> 00:24:16,880
but where else can you possibly fly to?

411
00:24:23,610 --> 00:24:25,640
How's the translation team coming along?

412
00:24:25,640 --> 00:24:27,110
They're incredibly efficient.

413
00:24:27,110 --> 00:24:27,830
They finished the first batch of

414
00:24:27,830 --> 00:24:29,600
ordnance data translation in just a week.

415
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:30,200
That Jiang Xueting

416
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:31,260
really is a talent.

417
00:24:31,700 --> 00:24:33,900
He handled the core part
of the translation.

418
00:24:33,900 --> 00:24:34,740
At this rate,

419
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:35,830
all 3 batches should be done

420
00:24:35,830 --> 00:24:36,940
by the end of the month.

421
00:24:36,940 --> 00:24:39,340
[Army Commander's Office]

422
00:24:38,290 --> 00:24:39,160
Once the materials are ready,

423
00:24:39,160 --> 00:24:40,200
we can call a meeting

424
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:41,400
with those veterans.

425
00:24:46,250 --> 00:24:47,000
Surprise.

426
00:24:48,170 --> 00:24:49,370
What brings you here?

427
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:50,770
What,

428
00:24:51,530 --> 00:24:53,460
are you not happy to see me?

429
00:24:53,700 --> 00:24:54,500
Of course I am.

430
00:24:56,590 --> 00:24:58,720
Why didn't you tell me you were coming?

431
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:01,160
If I didn't come,

432
00:25:01,180 --> 00:25:02,970
I'm afraid my boyfriend

433
00:25:03,160 --> 00:25:04,820
would grow wings and fly away.

434
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:06,270
How could I?

435
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:08,530
Why did you come straight here

436
00:25:08,530 --> 00:25:10,660
instead of coming to my place to see me?

437
00:25:10,820 --> 00:25:11,820
Well, I wanted to,

438
00:25:12,330 --> 00:25:14,220
but 9 times out of 10, you're not there

439
00:25:14,220 --> 00:25:16,090
whenever I visit your residence.

440
00:25:16,960 --> 00:25:17,740
My fault.

441
00:25:18,530 --> 00:25:20,860
I haven't spent much time with you lately.

442
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:24,420
I understand.

443
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:26,920
You just took command of the Ninth Army

444
00:25:26,920 --> 00:25:27,640
and have to help your father

445
00:25:27,640 --> 00:25:29,530
handle all those
complicated military affairs,

446
00:25:29,530 --> 00:25:31,330
out early and home late every day.

447
00:25:31,330 --> 00:25:32,280
I made you

448
00:25:32,310 --> 00:25:34,090
some duck soup
with reishi mushrooms and red dates

449
00:25:34,090 --> 00:25:36,350
to help you recover from all the fatigue.

450
00:25:44,270 --> 00:25:45,530
I simmered it

451
00:25:45,560 --> 00:25:46,640
for a full 8 hours.

452
00:25:49,770 --> 00:25:51,100
Why cook it yourself?

453
00:25:51,120 --> 00:25:52,920
There're plenty of cooks at home.

454
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:54,500
That's not the same thing at all.

455
00:25:54,500 --> 00:25:56,180
No matter how well someone else cooks,

456
00:25:56,180 --> 00:25:57,510
it can't replace

457
00:25:58,880 --> 00:26:00,540
the love and care I put into it.

458
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:09,930
It's hot.

459
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,460
I never would've guessed,

460
00:26:22,610 --> 00:26:23,270
Second Young Lady Tao—

461
00:26:23,270 --> 00:26:25,070
besides being a great dancer,

462
00:26:25,830 --> 00:26:27,560
you're also an excellent cook.

463
00:26:29,110 --> 00:26:30,180
That's why

464
00:26:30,590 --> 00:26:33,070
you really are a lucky man.

465
00:26:35,900 --> 00:26:37,100
Couldn't agree more.

466
00:26:39,750 --> 00:26:41,610
Military affairs are important,

467
00:26:41,660 --> 00:26:42,330
but you also have to

468
00:26:42,330 --> 00:26:43,510
take good care of yourself, too.

469
00:26:43,040 --> 00:26:47,280
[Army Commander's Office]

470
00:26:44,440 --> 00:26:45,110
I will.

471
00:26:46,750 --> 00:26:48,110
Sometime soon,

472
00:26:48,290 --> 00:26:50,820
my father wants to invite you over
for dinner.

473
00:26:52,550 --> 00:26:53,040
Sure.

474
00:26:54,640 --> 00:26:56,190
[Secretariat]

475
00:26:55,790 --> 00:26:56,450
Commander.

476
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:04,010
It's you.

477
00:27:05,060 --> 00:27:06,030
Why are you here?

478
00:27:07,860 --> 00:27:08,340
What,

479
00:27:08,630 --> 00:27:09,740
you two know each other?

480
00:27:09,740 --> 00:27:10,510
He...

481
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:14,920
He's my newly hired translation secretary,

482
00:27:14,920 --> 00:27:15,780
Jiang Xueting.

483
00:27:19,090 --> 00:27:21,560
A translation... secretary?

484
00:27:23,410 --> 00:27:24,670
This is my girlfriend,

485
00:27:24,880 --> 00:27:25,440
Tao Ziyi.

486
00:27:27,810 --> 00:27:28,340
Miss Tao.

487
00:27:29,010 --> 00:27:30,380
I owe you an apology
for the way I treated you

488
00:27:30,380 --> 00:27:31,910
outside the girls' school.

489
00:27:33,360 --> 00:27:35,220
You two have that kind of history?

490
00:27:37,750 --> 00:27:39,750
Secretary Jiang enjoys lecturing people.

491
00:27:39,750 --> 00:27:40,850
I can do without

492
00:27:41,280 --> 00:27:42,630
that kind of history.

493
00:27:45,720 --> 00:27:46,380
Commander.

494
00:27:49,190 --> 00:27:50,750
If there's nothing else,

495
00:27:50,780 --> 00:27:52,310
I'll head back to my office.

496
00:27:54,920 --> 00:27:57,800
[Secretariat] [Inspector General's Office]

497
00:28:02,700 --> 00:28:03,550
Mr. Yu.

498
00:28:08,670 --> 00:28:10,270
Did you really not know

499
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:11,810
that this Jiang Xueting

500
00:28:11,880 --> 00:28:13,490
is Ye Pingjun's boyfriend?

501
00:28:13,980 --> 00:28:15,230
I really didn't know—

502
00:28:15,810 --> 00:28:17,540
until Li Boren told me about it.

503
00:28:19,030 --> 00:28:20,160
What a coincidence.

504
00:28:20,880 --> 00:28:21,700
When he went

505
00:28:21,750 --> 00:28:24,490
to pick up Ye Pingjun from school before,

506
00:28:24,980 --> 00:28:25,940
we had

507
00:28:26,350 --> 00:28:27,790
a bit of a clash.

508
00:28:29,380 --> 00:28:30,290
I see.

509
00:28:31,840 --> 00:28:32,910
Was hiring him

510
00:28:33,240 --> 00:28:34,750
really just a coincidence?

511
00:28:34,750 --> 00:28:35,790
Not at all.

512
00:28:37,300 --> 00:28:39,630
I chose him after careful consideration.

513
00:28:39,740 --> 00:28:40,940
If you'd seen his resume,

514
00:28:40,940 --> 00:28:41,680
you'd know

515
00:28:42,220 --> 00:28:43,000
that he's truly

516
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:44,140
a rare talent.

517
00:28:46,790 --> 00:28:47,420
Really?

518
00:28:49,290 --> 00:28:50,890
Don't you trust my judgment?

519
00:28:58,480 --> 00:28:59,010
Xueting,

520
00:28:59,160 --> 00:29:00,220
you're still here?

521
00:29:00,660 --> 00:29:01,390
Team Leader.

522
00:29:01,570 --> 00:29:03,740
I've only got 2 pages left to finish here.

523
00:29:03,740 --> 00:29:05,400
Why don't you give me your files?

524
00:29:05,400 --> 00:29:07,350
I'll archive them all together in a bit.

525
00:29:07,350 --> 00:29:07,680
Okay.

526
00:29:08,110 --> 00:29:08,500
Here.

527
00:29:08,900 --> 00:29:10,230
Thanks for the trouble.

528
00:29:10,680 --> 00:29:11,680
See you tomorrow.

529
00:29:11,680 --> 00:29:12,680
See you tomorrow.

530
00:29:56,700 --> 00:30:00,380
[Archives]

531
00:30:08,720 --> 00:30:09,290
Hello.

532
00:30:14,590 --> 00:30:16,070
I'm new here and not quite
familiar with things yet.

533
00:30:16,070 --> 00:30:16,940
Could you help me check

534
00:30:16,940 --> 00:30:17,550
if these documents

535
00:30:17,550 --> 00:30:18,810
are in the right place?

536
00:30:18,920 --> 00:30:19,720
Leave it to me.

537
00:30:19,790 --> 00:30:20,940
You can head back first.

538
00:30:20,940 --> 00:30:22,000
Much appreciated.

539
00:30:30,690 --> 00:30:35,340
[Archives]

540
00:30:47,400 --> 00:30:47,900
Wu.

541
00:30:47,930 --> 00:30:49,090
Turn around and
go back to the headquarters.

542
00:30:49,090 --> 00:30:50,200
I forgot a document.

543
00:30:50,200 --> 00:30:51,170
Yes, Commander.

544
00:31:40,410 --> 00:31:42,740
[Nanhai Military General
Staff Department]

545
00:32:11,170 --> 00:32:12,410
[File on the Register of Fallen Soldiers]

546
00:32:13,520 --> 00:32:14,610
[File on the Register of Fallen Soldiers]

547
00:32:23,010 --> 00:32:24,790
[Exclusively for
Nanhuai Army Headquarters]

548
00:32:24,820 --> 00:32:27,320
[List of Fallen Soldiers]
[Wang Yichuan, Lu Baichuan, Liu Bowen]

549
00:32:45,830 --> 00:32:46,830
Secretary Jiang.

550
00:32:48,090 --> 00:32:49,000
It's so late.

551
00:32:49,740 --> 00:32:51,070
What are you doing here?

552
00:32:51,090 --> 00:32:51,830
Commander.

553
00:32:52,750 --> 00:32:53,990
Recently, I've been busy translating

554
00:32:53,990 --> 00:32:55,720
the German M18 submachine gun.

555
00:32:56,240 --> 00:32:58,240
I specifically applied to
Team Leader Bao and Staff Officer Li

556
00:32:58,240 --> 00:33:00,170
for access to relevant materials.

557
00:33:08,460 --> 00:33:10,430
[German Weapons]

558
00:33:19,770 --> 00:33:21,430
Secretary Jiang, do you think

559
00:33:21,560 --> 00:33:24,420
the reference materials
collected by the military

560
00:33:24,530 --> 00:33:25,730
are fairly accurate?

561
00:33:27,430 --> 00:33:29,030
They're sufficient for now,

562
00:33:29,030 --> 00:33:29,650
but

563
00:33:30,790 --> 00:33:31,330
I'd suggest

564
00:33:31,330 --> 00:33:32,930
increasing the update frequency

565
00:33:32,930 --> 00:33:34,860
to ensure they remain up-to-date.

566
00:33:39,200 --> 00:33:42,290
[German Weapons]

567
00:33:45,480 --> 00:33:46,540
You've got a point.

568
00:33:51,040 --> 00:33:52,440
If there's nothing else,

569
00:33:52,740 --> 00:33:54,600
I'll head back to my office first.

570
00:34:21,270 --> 00:34:23,730
[List of Fallen Soldiers]
[Liu Shan, Zhang Jianbing, Chen Xuan]

571
00:34:34,460 --> 00:34:40,530
[Nanhuai Orphanage]

572
00:34:41,280 --> 00:34:47,960
[Shelter the Orphans,
Uphold Compassion and Justice]

573
00:34:44,150 --> 00:34:44,810
Lend a hand.

574
00:34:45,920 --> 00:34:46,570
Madam Yu.

575
00:34:46,710 --> 00:34:47,500
Fifth Young Master Yu.

576
00:34:47,500 --> 00:34:48,570
Thank you for coming in person

577
00:34:48,570 --> 00:34:50,030
to visit the orphans here.

578
00:34:50,780 --> 00:34:51,820
If you hadn't stepped forward

579
00:34:51,820 --> 00:34:53,380
to negotiate with
the cotton mill this time,

580
00:34:53,380 --> 00:34:53,960
they wouldn't have agreed

581
00:34:53,960 --> 00:34:55,710
to give up these dormitories.

582
00:34:56,380 --> 00:34:57,420
I came today

583
00:34:57,630 --> 00:34:59,600
to discuss with you

584
00:34:59,880 --> 00:35:02,300
the follow-up work for the orphanage.

585
00:35:02,500 --> 00:35:04,180
I brought some hygiene products

586
00:35:02,930 --> 00:35:04,570
[Shelter the Orphans,
Uphold Compassion and Justice]

587
00:35:04,190 --> 00:35:05,990
for the children to keep on hand.

588
00:35:06,380 --> 00:35:07,570
Thank you so much.

589
00:35:09,940 --> 00:35:11,380
Let me introduce.

590
00:35:13,980 --> 00:35:15,360
This is the director of Chunfeng Troupe,

591
00:35:15,360 --> 00:35:16,860
Liang Wenbo.

592
00:35:17,090 --> 00:35:18,050
Hello, Madam Yu.

593
00:35:18,380 --> 00:35:19,710
Hello, Director Liang.

594
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:21,000
You're truly young and promising.

595
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:21,860
You flatter me.

596
00:35:22,710 --> 00:35:23,460
This is the troupe's playwright,

597
00:35:23,460 --> 00:35:25,340
Miss Ye Pingjun.

598
00:35:25,500 --> 00:35:26,300
Hello.

599
00:35:26,880 --> 00:35:27,900
After the location of the orphanage

600
00:35:27,900 --> 00:35:28,730
was finalized,

601
00:35:28,780 --> 00:35:29,760
they've been coming over to help

602
00:35:29,760 --> 00:35:30,880
with moving, cleaning,

603
00:35:30,880 --> 00:35:33,300
and running around
taking care of everything.

604
00:35:33,300 --> 00:35:34,670
So you're Ye Pingjun.

605
00:35:34,760 --> 00:35:36,110
I've read about you in the newspaper.

606
00:35:36,110 --> 00:35:36,710
I finally

607
00:35:36,710 --> 00:35:38,210
get to meet you in person today.

608
00:35:38,210 --> 00:35:39,700
Hello, I'm Yu Qixuan.

609
00:35:39,880 --> 00:35:41,480
I'm officially your fan now.

610
00:35:42,060 --> 00:35:43,390
Thank you, Miss Qixuan.

611
00:35:44,320 --> 00:35:46,510
Thank you young people

612
00:35:46,650 --> 00:35:47,530
for fighting so hard

613
00:35:47,530 --> 00:35:49,530
to secure the Charity Union's vote.

614
00:35:49,550 --> 00:35:51,060
Your efforts alone

615
00:35:51,570 --> 00:35:53,500
turned the tide at the last minute.

616
00:35:53,500 --> 00:35:54,000
Madam Yu.

617
00:35:54,000 --> 00:35:55,530
It was the least we could do.

618
00:35:56,780 --> 00:35:58,170
Miss Ye is renowned for

619
00:35:58,170 --> 00:36:00,430
her outstanding talent and compassion.

620
00:36:00,940 --> 00:36:02,510
What's even more remarkable

621
00:36:02,510 --> 00:36:03,900
is that her quick wit

622
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:05,150
is just as brilliant as

623
00:36:05,150 --> 00:36:06,350
the plays she writes.

624
00:36:06,480 --> 00:36:09,340
I've had the privilege of
witnessing it firsthand.

625
00:36:13,190 --> 00:36:13,760
Pingjun.

626
00:36:14,500 --> 00:36:15,460
The bedding sent by the Charity Union

627
00:36:15,460 --> 00:36:16,800
has all been registered.

628
00:36:16,800 --> 00:36:17,960
Over here, Lan Qing.

629
00:36:31,620 --> 00:36:32,370
Madam Yu.

630
00:36:34,270 --> 00:36:35,330
First Young Madam.

631
00:36:37,190 --> 00:36:38,500
Long time no see.

632
00:36:39,580 --> 00:36:41,020
How have you been?

633
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:42,990
Very well,

634
00:36:43,160 --> 00:36:43,960
thanks to you.

635
00:36:46,830 --> 00:36:47,560
Madam Yu,

636
00:36:47,660 --> 00:36:49,190
the reception room is ready.

637
00:36:49,190 --> 00:36:49,650
Please.

638
00:36:49,770 --> 00:36:50,460
Alright.

639
00:36:57,290 --> 00:37:00,670
[Reception Room]

640
00:36:57,570 --> 00:36:59,070
The shower room has been repaired.

641
00:36:59,070 --> 00:37:00,630
It opens once a day.

642
00:37:01,030 --> 00:37:03,320
The heating equipment is donated by
the Chamber of Commerce.

643
00:37:03,320 --> 00:37:04,190
As for the infirmary,

644
00:37:04,190 --> 00:37:05,960
there's a doctor on duty regularly.

645
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:06,760
Right.

646
00:37:07,070 --> 00:37:09,850
The kids are young and frail,

647
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:10,820
so they need

648
00:37:10,820 --> 00:37:13,350
a doctor stationed here
on a permanent basis.

649
00:37:14,260 --> 00:37:15,320
I'll go talk to

650
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:18,080
the Department of Health

651
00:37:18,080 --> 00:37:18,940
about this.

652
00:37:20,530 --> 00:37:22,260
Thank you so much, Madam Yu.

653
00:37:22,760 --> 00:37:23,360
Director,

654
00:37:23,630 --> 00:37:25,150
if the kids need anything,

655
00:37:25,360 --> 00:37:27,490
feel free to call us at Yu's Residence.

656
00:37:27,630 --> 00:37:28,230
Thank you.

657
00:37:34,130 --> 00:37:35,190
First Young Madam.

658
00:37:35,590 --> 00:37:38,120
If you have something to say,
please go ahead.

659
00:37:38,570 --> 00:37:40,280
I heard you're still performing

660
00:37:40,280 --> 00:37:41,480
at Yuchun Theater,

661
00:37:42,630 --> 00:37:45,030
and Changxuan often goes
to see your shows.

662
00:37:45,230 --> 00:37:46,480
Since you already know,

663
00:37:46,480 --> 00:37:47,570
why ask?

664
00:37:49,340 --> 00:37:50,150
I know you lost your child

665
00:37:50,150 --> 00:37:51,330
back then,

666
00:37:52,440 --> 00:37:53,120
and I know

667
00:37:53,150 --> 00:37:54,550
that was your only child.

668
00:37:56,380 --> 00:37:58,240
I understand why you hold a grudge

669
00:37:59,190 --> 00:38:00,450
against the Yu family.

670
00:38:04,510 --> 00:38:05,940
That's why I came to speak with you.

671
00:38:05,940 --> 00:38:07,400
What are you trying to say?

672
00:38:13,330 --> 00:38:14,660
I'm saying that

673
00:38:15,050 --> 00:38:17,180
things ended so tragically

674
00:38:18,330 --> 00:38:20,160
when you were with Mingxuan.

675
00:38:20,640 --> 00:38:22,260
Now Changxuan is the Yu family's

676
00:38:22,260 --> 00:38:23,710
only male heir,

677
00:38:24,050 --> 00:38:24,880
and the one my father-in-law

678
00:38:24,880 --> 00:38:26,230
values most as his successor.

679
00:38:26,230 --> 00:38:28,230
Don't you think it's inappropriate

680
00:38:28,550 --> 00:38:30,550
for you to be getting so close to him?

681
00:38:31,550 --> 00:38:33,340
You don't need to tell me that.

682
00:38:34,090 --> 00:38:36,980
Fifth Young Master Yu loves opera
and enjoys supporting us performers.

683
00:38:36,980 --> 00:38:37,480
If you want to

684
00:38:37,480 --> 00:38:38,630
tie his hands,

685
00:38:39,360 --> 00:38:40,690
go tell him yourselves.

686
00:38:57,870 --> 00:38:58,360
Miss.

687
00:38:59,130 --> 00:39:00,440
Make sure to check the medicines

688
00:39:00,440 --> 00:39:01,710
we've stocked for you regularly

689
00:39:01,710 --> 00:39:03,050
and verify their expiration dates.

690
00:39:02,150 --> 00:39:05,150
[Sterile Bandages][Iodine Tincture]

691
00:39:03,510 --> 00:39:05,040
Okay, we'll remember that.

692
00:39:05,100 --> 00:39:05,960
Go back to work.

693
00:39:06,820 --> 00:39:08,880
If you worked in a hospital, Jinxuan,

694
00:39:08,900 --> 00:39:09,530
you'd definitely be

695
00:39:09,530 --> 00:39:10,790
a great pediatrician.

696
00:39:11,780 --> 00:39:12,320
Put it here.

697
00:39:12,320 --> 00:39:13,590
When you have a child,

698
00:39:13,980 --> 00:39:15,580
I'll help you take care of it.

699
00:39:16,380 --> 00:39:17,900
Something's happened!
Something's happened!

700
00:39:17,900 --> 00:39:19,610
Manager, where's the medical kit?

701
00:39:19,610 --> 00:39:20,860
What's wrong? Is someone hurt?

702
00:39:20,860 --> 00:39:22,110
A box in the courtyard
wasn't stacked properly.

703
00:39:22,110 --> 00:39:22,630
It fell

704
00:39:22,730 --> 00:39:24,930
and hit a girl from the Chunfeng Troupe.

705
00:39:42,510 --> 00:39:48,080
[Nursery]

706
00:39:57,730 --> 00:39:58,460
Does it hurt?

707
00:39:58,850 --> 00:40:00,600
[Slippery Floor]

708
00:39:59,070 --> 00:39:59,800
A little bit.

709
00:40:46,490 --> 00:40:47,030
It's done.

710
00:40:47,030 --> 00:40:49,270
[Slippery Floor]

711
00:40:47,420 --> 00:40:47,950
I'll go put the medicine away.

712
00:40:47,950 --> 00:40:48,780
Thank you.

713
00:40:53,840 --> 00:40:54,780
Mr. Yu.

714
00:41:04,690 --> 00:41:05,820
Can I help you?

715
00:41:07,480 --> 00:41:08,340
No, not really.

716
00:41:09,550 --> 00:41:11,150
My mom asked me to come and ask

717
00:41:12,010 --> 00:41:13,090
if the kids need anything else

718
00:41:13,090 --> 00:41:14,350
for their daily needs.

719
00:41:14,840 --> 00:41:17,500
She'll have someone prepare it
and send it over.

720
00:41:17,690 --> 00:41:18,320
No need.

721
00:41:18,670 --> 00:41:19,510
What Madam Yu has prepared

722
00:41:19,510 --> 00:41:20,380
is already more than enough.

723
00:41:20,380 --> 00:41:21,710
Please thank her for me.

724
00:41:26,940 --> 00:41:27,280
Okay.

725
00:41:27,280 --> 00:41:28,210
Go get some rest.

726
00:41:29,030 --> 00:41:30,290
Alright, I'm off then.

727
00:41:54,380 --> 00:41:54,960
Jinxuan.

728
00:41:56,450 --> 00:41:57,780
You're still up so late.

729
00:41:57,960 --> 00:41:59,220
Changxuan, aren't you

730
00:41:59,230 --> 00:42:00,690
also working hard so late?

731
00:42:09,550 --> 00:42:11,680
Pear, snow fungus, and lily bulb soup.

732
00:42:11,820 --> 00:42:12,460
You used to make this for me

733
00:42:12,460 --> 00:42:14,120
all the time when I was little.

734
00:42:21,070 --> 00:42:23,000
Why are you looking at me like that?

735
00:42:23,730 --> 00:42:25,060
At the orphanage today,

736
00:42:25,790 --> 00:42:27,450
you were acting very strange.

737
00:42:28,360 --> 00:42:29,290
What do you mean?

738
00:42:29,510 --> 00:42:30,610
I can tell

739
00:42:31,300 --> 00:42:32,960
you care about Miss Ye.

740
00:42:38,980 --> 00:42:39,340
Jinxuan.

741
00:42:39,340 --> 00:42:40,470
You must be kidding.

742
00:42:42,280 --> 00:42:43,050
Changxuan.

743
00:42:44,290 --> 00:42:45,710
Your eyes gave you away.

744
00:42:49,550 --> 00:42:50,840
I already have Ziyi.

745
00:42:58,580 --> 00:43:00,190
A marriage of convenience—

746
00:43:01,710 --> 00:43:02,190
I've already done that for our Yu family,

747
00:43:02,190 --> 00:43:03,250
and that's enough.

748
00:43:05,030 --> 00:43:06,820
I hope you and Qixuan

749
00:43:06,860 --> 00:43:08,990
can both spend your lives with someone

750
00:43:09,010 --> 00:43:10,050
you truly love.

751
00:43:16,730 --> 00:43:18,380
My greatest regret in life

752
00:43:20,090 --> 00:43:21,970
is that I never fought

753
00:43:22,420 --> 00:43:24,230
against my own fate

754
00:43:28,380 --> 00:43:30,640
and lost the person I cherished the most.

755
00:43:34,820 --> 00:43:36,080
After all these years,

756
00:43:37,710 --> 00:43:38,460
Brother-in-law still hasn't

757
00:43:38,460 --> 00:43:39,990
found a place in your heart.

758
00:43:42,760 --> 00:43:44,760
Sooner or later, you'll understand

759
00:43:45,400 --> 00:43:46,860
that feelings

760
00:43:48,480 --> 00:43:50,340
have nothing to do with time.

761
00:43:56,960 --> 00:43:58,020
It's getting late.

762
00:43:58,690 --> 00:43:59,550
Get some rest.

763
00:44:10,530 --> 00:44:11,230
Changxuan.

764
00:44:14,380 --> 00:44:16,860
Be honest with yourself
about your feelings.

765
00:44:16,860 --> 00:44:18,590
Once you let someone slip away,

766
00:44:21,000 --> 00:44:22,130
you may lose them for good.
